


      Russian Cream

      6 servings

      1 C    whipping cream
      1/2 C  sugar
      1 T    gelatine
      1/2 C  cold water
      1 pint sour cream
      1 t    vanilla

      Heat whipping cream and sugar in a double boiler with
      stirring until warm and sugar is dissolved.  At the 
      same time, dissolve gelatine in cold water.  Remove cream
      from heat, add gelatine, and let cool a little until
      luke-warm.  Add sour cream and stir with a whisk until 
      smooth.  Add vanilla.  Chill.

      Serve with rapsberry sauce: Puree frozen rapsberries and
      a little sugar or fresh berries with a little more sugar.

      Makes six servings.  

      Probably one envelope of gelatine is enough; this is a 
      little less than one tablespoon.

